c division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{4x-1}{x+1} = 4 -\\dfrac{5}{x+1}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{1}\\frac{4x - 1}{x + 1}dx &= \\int_{0}^{1}(4 - \\frac{5}{x + 1})dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{1}4dx - 5\\int_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x + 1}dx \\\\\n&= \\left.4x\\right|_{0}^{1} - 5\\ln \\mid x + \\left.1 \\mid \\right|_{0}^{1} \\\\\n&= [4 - 0] - 5[\\ln 2 - \\ln 1] \\\\\n&= 4 - 5\\ln 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186064103 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186064103 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3}\\,\\textrm d x.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186064103 1074 "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{2x^{2} - 3x - 4}{x - 3}dx &= \\int(2x + 3 + \\frac{5}{x - 3})dx \\\\\n&= x^{2} + 3x + 5\\ln \\mid x - 3 \\mid + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186064103 1074 "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division. \n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | $x^2$ | $x^1$ | $x^0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color{red}3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $\\color{gray}\\downarrow$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac{ 2x^2-3x-4}{x-3} = 2x + 3 + \\dfrac {5}{x-3} .\n\t}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-