row$ | $\\dfrac12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-\\dfrac12$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} & =1-\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2(x-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{2x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x-1}{2x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (1-\\frac{1}{2x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[x-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x-1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186064105 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186064105 1071 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186064105 1074 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x$. Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}u = x & ⟹u^{′} = 1 \\\\ v^{′} = e^{7x} & ⟹v = \\frac{1}{7}e^{7x}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intuv^{′}dx &= uv - \\intvu^{′}dx \\\\\n\\intx \\cdot e^{7x}dx &= x \\cdot \\frac{1}{7}e^{7x} - \\int\\frac{1}{7}e^{7x} \\cdot 1dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intxe^{7x}dx &= \\frac{1}{7}xe^{7x} - \\frac{1}{7}\\inte^{7x}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}xe^{7x} - \\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{e^{7x}}{7}) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{7}xe^{7x} - \\frac{1}{49}e^{7x} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186064105 1074 "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x