places." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186083032 1071 "A data set has mean $\\overline{x}=15$ and variance $\\sigma^2=3.25$. Find the $z$-score of an observation $x=17.3,$ giving your answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186083032 1074 "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz = \\frac{x-\\overline{x}}{\\sigma}\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is\n\n$$\n\\overline{x}=15\n$$\n\nand we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma = \\sqrt{\\sigma^2} = \\sqrt{3.25}\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=17.3$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= (x - x^(―))/(σ) \\\\\n&\\approx \\frac{17.3 - 15}{\\sqrt{3.25}} \\\\\n&\\approx 1.28\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186083032 1074 "The $z$-score of an observation $x$ is defined by\n\n$$\nz = \\frac{x-\\overline{x}}{\\sigma}.\n$$\n\nThe $z$-score represents how many standard deviations an observation is above or below the mean of the data set.\n\nHere, we're told that the mean is $\\overline{x}=15,$ and we can calculate the standard deviation as\n\n$$\n\\sigma = \\sqrt{\\sigma^2} = \\sqrt{3.25}.\n$$\n\nSo, the $z$-score of the observation $x=17.3$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\frac{x-\\overset{―}{x}}{\\sigma } \\\\  & ≈\\frac{17.3-15}{\\sqrt{3.25}} \\\\  & ≈1.28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto $2$ decimal places." 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186083033 1071 "A data set has a standard deviation $\\sigma=1.2$ and an unknown mean. An observation of the data set has the value $x=13.2$ and $z$-score $z=-1.5$. Find the mean of the data set." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186083033 1071 "A data set has a standard deviation $\\sigma=1.2$ and an unknown mean. An observation of the data set has the value $x=13.2$ and $z$-score $z=-1.5.$ Find the mean of the data set." 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186083033 1074 "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overline{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma$, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx = \\overline{x} + z \\cdot \\sigma\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=13.2$, $z=-1.5$, and $\\sigma=1.2$ into the formula and solving for $\\overline{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= x^(―) + z \\cdot σ \\\\\n13.2 &= x^(―) + (-1.5) \\cdot 1.2 \\\\\n13.2 &= x^(―) - 1.8 \\\\\nx^(―) &= 13.2 + 1.8 \\\\\nx^(―) &= 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186083033 1074 "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overline{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx = \\overline{x} + z \\cdot \\sigma\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=13.2,$ $z=-1.5,$ and $\\sigma=1.2$ into the formula and solving for $\\overline{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 13.2 & =\\overset{―}{x}+(-1.5)\\cdot 1.2 \\\\ 13.2 & =\\overset{―}{x}-1.8 \\\\ \\overset{―}{x} & =13.2+1.8 \\\\ \\overset{―}{x} & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186083037 1071 "Evaluate ${}_{7}C_5$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186083037 1071 "Evaluate ${}_{7}C_5.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186083037 1074 "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_nC_r = \\dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!r!}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=7$ and $r=5$, we get\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\begin{aligned} {}_{7}C_5 &= \\dfrac {7!} {(7 - 5)!5!} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {7!} {2!5!} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {7 \\cdot 6 \\cdot \\cancel{5!}} {2!\\cancel{5!}} \\\\[5pt] &= \\dfrac {7 \\cdot 6} {2 \\cdot 1} \\\\[5pt] & = \\dfrac {42}{2} \\\\[5pt] &= 21. \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186083037 1074 "The number of combinations 