194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186083044 1071 "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ with real coefficients has roots $z_1=3+\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3-\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $f(z).$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186083044 1074 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}z_1=3+\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}z_2=3-\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nand the coefficient of the quadratic term is\n\n$$\n{\\color{black}a=2}\n$$\n\nwe can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na(z - z_{1})(z - z_{2}) &= 2(z - (3 + \\textrm{i}))(z - (3 - \\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(z - (3 + \\textrm{i}))(z - (3 - \\textrm{i})) &= 2(z^{2} - (3 + \\textrm{i})z - (3 - \\textrm{i})z + (3 + \\textrm{i})(3 - \\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - (3 + \\textrm{i} + 3 - \\textrm{i})z + (3^{2} - \\textrm{i}^{2})) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - 6z + (9 + 1)) \\\\\n&= 2(z^{2} - 6z + 10) \\\\\n&= 2z^{2} - 12z + 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(z) = 2z^2-12z+20\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186083044 1074 "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}z_1=3+\\textrm{i}}$ and ${\\color{black}z_2=3-\\textrm{i}},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=2},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) & =2(z-(3+\\text{i}))(z-(3-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(z-(3+\\text{i}))(z-(3-\\text{i})) & =2({z}^{2}-(3+\\text{i})z-(3-\\text{i})z+(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-(3+\\text{i}+3-\\text{i})z+({3}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-6z+(9+1)) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-6z+10) \\\\  & =2{z}^{2}-12z+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z) = 2z^2-12z+20.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186083045 1071 "Factor $u^2-2u+10$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [1759