igin, as shown below. Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$, that traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(2,0)$.\n\n![](images/15/156d160267551e9dbf4db42b14b1e0dbb46ab658a836a760cf31a42eb89662d3.png)" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186087560 1071 "Consider the circle of radius $2$ centered at the origin, as shown below. Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi),$ that traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(2,0).$ \n\n![](images/15/156d160267551e9dbf4db42b14b1e0dbb46ab658a836a760cf31a42eb89662d3.png)" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186087560 1074 "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$ centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx = r\\cos\\theta, \\quad y = r\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r,0).$\n\nIn our case, the radius is $r = 2.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=2\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi).\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186087560 1074 "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the origin are\n\n$$\nx = r\\cos\\theta, \\quad y = r\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi)\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r,0)$.\n\nIn our case, the radius is $r = 2$. Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=2\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=2\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi)\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186087561 1071 "Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$, that generates a circle of radius $2$ centered at the point $(4,6)$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186087561 1071 "Construct a set of par