87582 1074 "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${\\color{black}x_1= 2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_{2,3}=-2\\pm \\textrm{i}}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is ${\\color{black}a=1}.$ \n\nTherefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x-(-2+\\text{i}))(x-(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-2-\\text{i})-x(-2+\\text{i})+(-2+\\text{i})(-2-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ (x-2)({x}^{2}+4x+5) & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+5x-2{x}^{2}-8x-10 & = \\\\ {x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x-10 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x) = x^3+2x^2-3x-10.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186087583 1071 "![](images/65/658fa5a494ef01b5924847335ce863aa8c6b5f8adee5ee97967a8c8bebd83a80.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x)$. Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186087583 1071 "![](images/65/658fa5a494ef01b5924847335ce863aa8c6b5f8adee5ee97967a8c8bebd83a80.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186087583 1074 "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x_1=-2}$, ${x_2=3}$, and\n\n$$\n{x_{3,4}=1 \\pm 3\\textrm{i}}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is ${a=1}$. Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= a(x - x_{1})(x - x_{2})(x - x_{3})(x - x_{4}) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot (x - (-2))(x - (3))(x - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(x - (1 - 3\\textrm{i})) \\\\\n&= (x + 2)(x - 3)(x - (1 + 3\\textrm{i}))(x - (1 - 3\\textrm{i}))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x + 2)(x - 3)(x - (1 + 3\\