rd basis vectors $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ under the action of  $\\mathbf T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ T(j) & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=2i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *horizontal* shear with a shear factor of $2.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186105624 1074 "We can find the images of the standard basis vectors $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ under the action of $\\mathbf T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nT(i) &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} = i \\\\\nT(j) &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} = 2i + j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a *horizontal* shear with a shear factor of $2$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186105625 1071 "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet ![](images/62/6231eb09a75376d694a6f47c47cf5a26aab4a32c28b2799f7e1f0825a7017f88.png) be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}.$ What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) under the action of $\\mathbf{T}?$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186105625 1071 "![](images/61/611f958a7bd7475e37f743ef86affde7754195fe2c9ad414e628c17a09d47e38.png)\n\nLet $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ be the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$. What is the image of the square $R$ (shown above) under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$?" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186105625 1074 "Looking at the matrix $T$, we can see that $\\mathbf{T}$ represents a vertical shear of 