ms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 11 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{5}{4}){R}_{1} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2} & ⟺ & \\,\\overset{{E}_{2}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot {E}_{1}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since $E_2E_1A=U,$ we can invert $E_2$ and $E_1$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{2}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ {E}_{1}A & ={E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}{E}_{2}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -\\frac{5}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & =([\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}])U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186119614 1071 "![](images/91/9129b6fbd360b9b9bcc937fd2acf0aedc25681d4b3dca100be7f681b7bb347dd.png) \n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $A$ given above, what is the value of $l_{42} \\cdot u_{24}?$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186119614 1071 "$\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 9 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIf $A=LU$ is the LU decomposition of