\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n![](images/15/151dc664a131df0f3e13f2997bb1af6d41586b5f4dcf8a1acd1342f85e1b9c92.png)" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186119618 1071 "Let $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186119618 1071 "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186119618 1074 "Multiplying each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}a &= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (-4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186119618 1074 "Multiplying each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}a & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186119619 1071 "Let $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 true] [17592186119619 1071 "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}$." 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186119619 1074 "First, we multiply each component of $\\mathb