early independent.\n\nSubstituting the given expressions for $p_1(t),p_2(t)$, and $p_3(t)$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}(1 + t) + x_{2}(-2t - 4) + x_{3}(-2t - 3) &= 0 \\\\\n(x_{1} - 4x_{2} - 3x_{3}) + (x_{1} - 2x_{2} - 2x_{3})t &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation is true for every $t$ if and only if\n\n$$\n{x_{1} - 4x_{2} - 3x_{3} = 0; x_{1} - 2x_{2} - 2x_{3} = 0\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{2} \\mid:=R_{2} + (-1)R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd. Hence, $x_3$ is a free variable. The system is now\n\n$$\n{x_{1} - 4x_{2} - 3x_{3} = 0; 2x_{2} + x_{3} = 0\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2=-\\dfrac 12x_3\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1-4\\left(-\\dfrac 12x_3\\right)-3x_3=0 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow \\qquad x_1=x_3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2} \\\\ x_{3}\\end{bmatrix}$\nFinally, for any\n\n$$\nx_3 \\neq 0\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x_2}{x_1}=\\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac 12x_3\\right)}{x_3}=-\\dfrac 12\n$$" 13194139533388 17592186045585 false] [17592186124306 1074 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist $x_1,x_2,x_3$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\nx_1p_1(t)+x_2p_2(t)+x_3p_3(t)=0.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if $x_1 = x_2 = x_3 = 0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the given expressions for $p_1(t),p_2(t),$ and $p_3(t)$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(1+t)+{x}_{2}(-2t-4)+{x}_{3}(-2t-3) & =0 \\\\ ({x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3})+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final equation is true for every $t$ if and only if \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}